{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794649666,"nonce":"ta8dbqI12hjBGywfrKwohN07HJU=","message":"Update from the iPhone (ef5d01d): the per-card textures are the baked CSS layers. The mobile runners never applied BlincConfig::motion_promotion, so a phone baked every bound node and CSS animation to a texture and blitted it; fixed in 2b32f600.\n\nThe 200 childless cards (cards_plain) now hold 145 MB at 59 fps and 0.53 cores, against 620 to 714 MB, 36 fps and 1.95 cores. The text cards are not helped much: opacity on a node with a child cannot be carried, so they are painted in full as before. At 100 cards 1660 MB became 1278 MB with the frame rate unchanged (render median 36.1 to 40.5 ms), at 60 cards 1192 became 1089 MB, at 20 cards no change, and 200 is still killed within 2 s on the build with the fix. So the memory per text card is not mainly the promotion setting; what allocates it is still open. The wanted fade for nodes that paint more than one draw is 82cb190.","files":null}]}